r used on a null value\n```\nThe initial exception occurs in:\n```text\nSliverReorderableListState._itemOffsetAt\nSliverReorderableListState._dragEnd\n_DragInfo.end\n```\n\nI also observed subsequent `Null check operator used on a null value` exceptions after the drop during later rebuilds. This matches the reported behavior. routing to the `team-framework` for further investigation.\n\n**Flutter Doctor Output**\n```dart\n[✓] Flutter (Channel stable, 3.47.5, on macOS 27.0 26A428 darwin-arm64, locale en-IN) [670ms]\n    • Flutter version 3.47.5 on channel stable at /Users/suryakommana/develop/flutter\n    • Upstream repository https://github.com/flutter/flutter.git\n    • Framework revision 6a19cca564 (11 days ago), 2026-09-17 14:13:22 -0400\n    • Engine revision af7e796e16\n    • Dart version 3.13.4\n    • DevTools version 2.60.0\n    • Feature flags: enable-web, enable-linux-desktop, enable-macos-desktop, enable-windows-desktop, enable-android, enable-ios, cli-animations, enable-native-assets,\n      enable-record-use, enable-swift-package-manager, omit-legacy-version-file, enable-lldb-debugging, enable-uiscene-migration\n\n[✓] Android toolchain - develop for Android devices (Android SDK version 36.0.0) [1,603ms]\n    • Android SDK at /Users/suryakommana/Library/Android/sdk\n    • Emulator version 37.1.11.0 (build_id 15917651) (CL:N/A)\n    • Platform android-37.0, build-tools 36.0.0\n    • Java binary at: /Applications/Android Studio.app/Contents/jbr/Contents/Home/bin/java\n      This is the JDK bundled with the latest Android Studio installation on this machine.\n      To manually set the JDK path, use: `flutter config --jdk-dir=\"path/to/jdk\"`.\n    • Java version OpenJDK Runtime Environment (build 25.0.2+-15348964-b329.117)\n    • All Android licenses accepted.\n\n[✓] Xcode - develop for iOS and macOS (Xcode 27.0) [760ms]\n    • Xcode at /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer\n    • Build 27A266a\n    • CocoaPods version 1.17.0\n\n[✓] Chrome - develop for